            <ArticleTitle>Coronary stenting with a balloon-expandable stent after the recanalization of chronic total occlusions.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>293-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>To diminish the restenosis rate after successful recanalization of chronic total coronary occlusion, we have implanted the Palmaz-Schatz stent in 6 patients. All procedures were successfully done without major complications. The angiographic follow-up at 6 months showed restenosis in one asymptomatic patient who had had 2 stents implanted. Five other patients had no evidence of restenosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
